= A measurement and its shadow

Every measurement leaves something outside the frame. We counted the bicycles that crossed the bridge, but not the riders who chose a different route because the crossing felt unsafe.

Our count rose by 18 percent after the protected lane opened. This suggests that the lane caused more people to cycle. The observation window covered two clear weeks in May; the earlier count took place during a rainy April.

The result is promising, but the counter cannot tell us whose journey became possible. That question calls for a different kind of evidence.
